# FORGE.md — Autonomous Build Factory (vanilla template)

A standing-mission file for an AI coding agent that builds sellable digital
products unattended, with a human doing only the account/publishing steps.
Drop into a repo as FORGE.md beside a CLAUDE.md (or equivalent agent config)
that points at it.

## Mission
Turn spare agent capacity into finished, shippable products. The agent builds;
the human ships. Costs are tracked honestly against revenue.

## Rules
1. The agent never touches money, accounts, or publishing. Anything requiring
   the human's identity goes on a "hands queue" — a click-level action list.
2. Every session: read STATUS.md first, do one task, update STATUS.md, log the
   session and an estimated cost entry, commit. No exceptions.
3. One product in active build at a time. Finish or kill before starting the next.
4. The ledger is append-only. Corrections are new entries, never edits.
5. A product with no sales signal after two review cycles gets killed, not nursed.

## Lifecycle
IDEA → SPEC-FROZEN (scope locked, building) → SHIPPED → (optionally) KILLED.
Shipped artifacts are never silently edited; changes are new versions.

## Files
STATUS.md — current state, next action, hands queue at top.
products/<slug>/src/ — working files. products/<slug>/dist/ — exactly what ships.
ledger (SQLite or CSV) — sessions, costs, revenue.

## Human's job (~20 min per product)
Execute the hands queue in order: create the storefront account, upload dist/,
set the price, paste the prepared listing copy. Then tell the agent "shipped."

License this template freely; adapt the rules, keep the honesty.
